                                    <version>1.6.0</version>
                                    <fixVersion>1.6.1</fixVersion>
                                    <component>parquet-mr</component>
                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14520078" author="rdblue" created="Wed, 29 Apr 2015 19:52:29 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fixed in #187. Had to downgrade the plugin dependency version to 3.16.0.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14520236" author="alexlevenson" created="Wed, 29 Apr 2015 21:03:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks like you beat me to it, I was doing the same thing. The scrooge folks are working on a fix so we can roll forward once that&apos;s out.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14520515" author="alexlevenson" created="Wed, 29 Apr 2015 23:29:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks like downgrading won&apos;t work for us.&lt;br/&gt;
Spoke with the scrooge folks and they are working on doing a release to fix the issue, but I think we are stuck until then.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14520519" author="alexlevenson" created="Wed, 29 Apr 2015 23:30:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Issue to watch:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/twitter/scrooge/issues/184&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/twitter/scrooge/issues/184&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Summary of the issue is the version we were using (3.17) depended on a snapshot that has been deleted (it was a bug that it depended on a snapshot)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14520532" author="rdblue" created="Wed, 29 Apr 2015 23:38:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m going to do the downgrade and ignore the failing tests. We know that the library works right as long as Scrooge does, so I think it is reasonable. I&apos;ll ping you on the PR for review.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17857231" author="rok" created="Sun, 23 Jun 2024 03:27:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This issue has been migrated to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-java/issues/1800&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;issue #1800&lt;/a&gt; on GitHub. Please see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2502&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;migration documentation&lt;/a&gt; for further details.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
